 𝐃𝐨𝐜𝐤𝐞𝐫: 𝐄𝐗𝐏𝐎𝐒𝐄 𝐯𝐬 -𝐩 

1️⃣ What 𝐄𝐗𝐏𝐎𝐒𝐄 Actually Does

- Documentation only — tells Docker: “my app listens on this port inside the container.”
- Doesn’t open the port on your host.

Useful for:
docker run -P → maps exposed ports to random host ports
Docker Compose port hints
Same network: containers can talk directly (no -p needed)


2️⃣ What -𝐩 Does

This is the real port mapping.

docker run -p 8080:8080 myapp

Host 8080 → container 8080
 Now you can access: http://localhost:8080

Remap ports:
docker run -p 3000:8080 myapp
Visit: http://localhost:3000

👇
EXPOSE → documentation
-p → publish port to host
